+lambda_1')/(lambda_1*(1+lambda_2'))."},{"line_end":402,"line_start":402,"support":"L = max{0, log(lambda_0) - 2*pi*|eta|}"}],"applicability":"The claim applies to the Hermitian regime (eta=0) with theta=0 and Phi=(sqrt(5)-1)/2. The formula is phase-spanning: positive output indicates localization, zero output indicates delocalization.","claim_id":"lyapunov_eta_zero","control_domains":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":82,"line_start":82,"support":"lambda_1=0.67, 0.435, 0.2 in the Hermitian quantum walk"},{"line_end":134,"line_start":134,"support":"we experimentally map the relationship between sigma and lambda_1, lambda_2 by scanning the whole parameter space"}],"control_name":"lambda_1","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"The source reports lambda_1 values 0.67, 0.435, 0.2 in the Hermitian phase diagram; the conservative interval [0.2, 0.67] lies within the source's 0-to-1 coupling range and is covered by the reported full-parameter-space phase scans.","maximum":0.67,"minimum":0.2},{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":82,"line_start":82,"support":"lambda_2=0.2, 0.435, 0.67 in the Hermitian quantum walk"},{"line_end":134,"line_start":134,"support":"we experimentally map the relationship between sigma and lambda_1, lambda_2 by scanning the whole parameter space"}],"control_name":"lambda_2","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"The source reports lambda_2 values 0.2, 0.435, 0.67 in the Hermitian phase diagram; the conservative interval [0.2, 0.67] lies within the source's 0-to-1 coupling range and is covered by the reported full-parameter-space phase scans.","maximum":0.67,"minimum":0.2}],"control_names":["lambda_1","lambda_2"],"depends_on":[],"fixed_condition_ids":["irrational_field_phi","theta_zero","eta_zero"],"mechanism_ids":["lambda0_structure"],"oracle_outputs":{"lyapunov_exponent":{"args":[{"param":"zero"},{"args":[{"args":[{"args":[{"var":"lambda_2"},{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"var":"lambda_1"},{"param":"square_exponent"}],"op":"power"}],"op":"subtract"},{"param":"sqrt_exponent"}],"op":"power"}],"op":"add"}],"op":"multiply"},{"args":[{"var":"lambda_1"},{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"args":[{"param":"one"},{"args":[{"var":"lambda_2"},{"param":"square_exponent"}],"op":"power"}],"op":"subtract"},{"param":"sqrt_exponent"}],"op":"power"}],"op":"add"}],"op":"multiply"}],"op":"divide"}],"op":"log"}],"op":"maximum"}},"quantitative_form":"L = max(0, log(lambda_0)) with lambda_0 = lambda_2*(1+sqrt(1-lambda_1^2))/(lambda_1*(1+sqrt(1-lambda_2^2)))","readout_names":["lyapunov_exponent"],"statement":"In the Hermitian regime (eta=0), the Lyapunov exponent of the UAMO is L = max(0, log(lambda_0)), where lambda_0 = lambda_2*(1+lambda_1')/(lambda_1*(1+lambda_2')). The positive versus zero output of this formula identifies localization versus delocalization across the full parameter square.","statistical_basis":"The Lyapunov exponent is a theoretical quantity; the source reports the formula and uses it to characterize the localization transition. The experimental phase diagram is measured via the standard deviation sigma at t=6.","uncertainty":"source_unspecified"},{"anchors":[{"line_end":402,"line_start":402,"support":"L = max{0, log(lambda_0) - 2*pi*|eta|}"},{"line_end":425,"line_start":425,"support":"We set theta=0, eta=0.1"},{"line_end":111,"line_start":111,"support":"lambda_0 = lambda_2*(1+lambda_1')/(lambda_1*(1+lambda_2'))"}],"applicability":"The claim applies to the non-Hermitian regime with eta=0.1, theta=0 and Phi=(sqrt(5)-1)/2. The formula is phase-spanning: positive output indicates localization, zero output indicates delocalization.","claim_id":"lyapunov_eta_point_one","control_domains":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":117,"line_start":117,"support":"lambda_1=0.5 and 0.25 in the non-Hermitian quantum walk"},{"line_end":418,"line_start":418,"support":"we experimentally measure the second moment ... as a function of